  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "7nzkxCV/spPzak/9PecCIHtj5L8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:19:20.973Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`packages/reactor/specs/tla/ReactorSync.tla` models the sync protocol in TLA+ and TLC checks it. The Phase-1 configuration is deliberately tiny \u2014 2 reactors (`r1`, `r2`), 1 document, 3 operations per reactor, bounded by `nextOpId <= 5` \u2014 and explores **357,574 distinct states (1,806,603 generated, max depth 42) in about 11 seconds.**\n\nFour **safety** invariants hold in every state explored:\n\n1. `TypeOK` \u2014 all variables well-typed;\n2. `OperationUniqueness` \u2014 no duplicate operation ids anywhere;\n3. `StreamMonotonicity` \u2014 operation indices within a stream never decrease;\n4. `CursorMonotonicity` \u2014 sync cursors never move backwards.\n\nThe **liveness** property, `EventualConsistency` (all reactors converge once nothing is in transit), is specified but **not checked** in Phase 1, because the unbounded temporal property is expensive. So \"verified\" here means safety only.\n\nWhat the model proves, in the authors' own framing: no data corruption, operation uniqueness within a stream, stream and cursor monotonicity, **idempotency** (an operation received repeatedly creates no duplicate), and that the reshuffle algorithm merges divergent streams deterministically by timestamp.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor/specs/tla/README.md` \u2014 Phase 1 Model; Properties Verified; What is Proven (Phase 1); Verification Results\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:19:20.973Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:19:20.973Z"
    }
  },
